<p>
  News Shuffle stores your shuffle filters, language and recently opened sites
  in this browser. You can remove those preferences by clearing this site’s data
  in your browser settings.
</p>
<p>
  Your browser requests site icons from Google, using each site’s hostname.
  Google receives the request and its connection details. See{" "}
  <ExternalLink
    class="text-foreground underline hover:text-primary transition-colors"
    href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
    locale="en"
  >
    Google’s privacy policy
  </ExternalLink>
  .
</p>
<p>
  When Google Analytics and Google AdSense are enabled, we use Analytics to
  measure page visits and use of the Shuffle button. Google can receive
  cookieless measurements while consent is denied. Shuffle events contain
  neither your selected filters nor the destination URL.
</p>
<p>
  Google and its advertising partners may use cookies to serve ads based on
  previous visits to this or other sites, subject to your privacy choices. If
  you see a consent message, use Privacy and cookie settings at the bottom of
  each page to change or withdraw your choice. Learn{" "}
  <ExternalLink
    class="text-foreground underline hover:text-primary transition-colors"
    href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
    locale="en"
  >
    how Google uses data from partner sites
  </ExternalLink>{" "}
  or adjust personalised ads in{" "}
  <ExternalLink
    class="text-foreground underline hover:text-primary transition-colors"
    href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
    locale="en"
  >
    Google Ads Settings
  </ExternalLink>
  .
</p>
<p>
  When you open a source, that website handles your visit under its own privacy
  practices.
</p>
<p>
  For questions, email{" "}
  <a
    class="text-foreground underline hover:text-primary transition-colors"
    href="mailto:privacy@mickschroeder.com"
  >
    privacy@mickschroeder.com
  </a>
  .
</p>
